 entity (a PostgreSQL table); rows list only attributes that drive behavior; the right column is the type.&lt;br&gt;PK = primary key (two PK rows form a composite key), FK = foreign key, UK = part of a unique constraint (Game: user_id + source_game_id;&lt;br&gt;Move: game_id + ply), idx = indexed column. A line is a relationship, read in the direction of its label. Crow&#x27;s-foot ends, repeated as text:&lt;br&gt;1 = exactly one (double bar); 0..N = zero or many (circle + fork); 1..N = one or many (bar + fork). Each text label sits at the end of the entity it describes." style="rounded=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=13;strokeColor=#999999;fillColor=#ffffff;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1010" width="1480" height="104" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>